==========
| Tokens |
==========
👉 A Token is the smallest individual unit of a C program that has a specific meaning to the compiler.

Types of Tokens in C
---------------------
👉 Keywords => Keywords are reserved words that have predefined meanings in C.
    int
    float
    char
    if
    else
    for
    while
    return
    break
    continue
    switch
    case
    void
    const

👉 Identifiers => Identifiers are names given to variables, functions, arrays, and other user-defined elements.
    age
    salary
    totalMarks
    sum
    studentName
Rules
------
  ✅ start Name letter or underscore (_).
  ✅ Digits come after this.
  ❌ No Space.
  ❌ No Keyword.

👉 Constants => A constant is a fixed value that does not change during program execution.
    100
    3.14
    'A'

👉 Strings => A string is a sequence of characters enclosed in double quotation marks.
    "Welcome"

👉 Operators => Operators are symbols used to perform operations on operands.
    +
    -
    *
    /
    %
    =
    ==
    >
    <
    >=
    <=
    &&
    ||

👉 Special Symbols => Special symbols are characters that have special meanings in C programs.
    ;
    {}
    ()
    []
    #
    ,

#include <stdio.h>
int main()
{
    int age = 20;
    printf("Age = %d", age);
    return 0;
}

========================
| Identify the Tokens |
=======================
_____________________________________________
| Token        | Type                       |
| ------------ | -------------------------- |
| `#include`   | Preprocessor Directive     |
| `stdio.h`    | Header File                |
| `int`        | Keyword                    |
| `main`       | Identifier                 |
| `(`          | Special Symbol             |
| `)`          | Special Symbol             |
| `{`          | Special Symbol             |
| `age`        | Identifier                 |
| `=`          | Operator                   |
| `20`         | Constant                   |
| `printf`     | Identifier (Function Name) |
| `"Age = %d"` | String                     |
| `;`          | Special Symbol             |
| `return`     | Keyword                    |
| `0`          | Constant                   |
| `}`          | Special Symbol             |
---------------------------------------------

Summary
--------
👉 A token is the smallest meaningful unit of a C program.
👉 The six main types of tokens are:
  👉 Keywords
  👉 Identifiers
  👉 Constants
  👉 Strings
  👉 Operators
  👉 Special Symbols
👉 Keywords are reserved words with predefined meanings.
👉 Identifiers are user-defined names for variables, functions, etc.
👉 Constants are fixed values that cannot change during execution.
👉 Strings are sequences of characters enclosed in double quotes.
👉 Operators perform operations on data.
👉 Special Symbols define the structure and syntax of a C program.
